WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.910
In Bogotá, a reader of Spanish
finds your Vue page all in English.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.690
The template is plain English, and
no plugin runs before the app mounts.

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:15.650
General Translation lets you register the
gt-vue plugin and wrap your template in T.

4
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.650
Install gt-vue, a 0.x release
whose API may still change.

5
00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:25.870
List your languages, register
the plugin before the app mounts,

6
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.730
and wrap the template in T.

7
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.450
Sign in, set your project ID,
and run npx gt translate.

8
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.830
Add a switcher built on useSetLocale,
which loads a language without a reload.

9
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:44.250
In Bogotá, the page switches in place
to Japanese, French and Spanish.
